Cell["\<\
The results show that parallelization significantly improves the runtime \
compared to the sequential brute force approach. Since the evaluation of each \
candidate number is independent, the workload can be distributed effectively \
across multiple Mathematica subkernels.

However, the underlying algorithmic structure remains unchanged. Even in the \
parallelized version, every number in the search range is still checked \
individually. Therefore, parallelization reduces the practical computation \
time, but it does not remove the fundamental scalability limitation of the \
brute force method.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9909722385875225`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e44abad7-c3d4-d141-b22e-\
a0a8a198569e"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "SlideShowNavigationBar",
 CellTags->
  "SlideShowHeader",ExpressionUUID->"95d7c69b-8396-9440-98db-56f1729685ee"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.3 Digit Permutation Class Approach", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6943454921732183`*^9, 3.6943455118916535`*^9}, 
   3.990952523195942*^9, {3.991661411983639*^9, 
   3.9916614120395193`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"51446a21-d1e2-4a37-b7a3-\
a9c59539edcb"],

Cell["\<\
A limitation of the brute force approach is that it checks numbers \
individually, even if several numbers consist of the same digits in a \
different order.

For Example 153, 315 and 531 have the same digit composition. Therefore, they \
also have the same digit power sum.

Corresponding Digit vector:
{0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0}
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6551323318137064`*^9, 3.655132346618133*^9}, {
   3.6558834788297663`*^9, 3.655883482105772*^9}, {3.655883581805547*^9, 
   3.655883589683561*^9}, {3.6558837346868153`*^9, 3.655883735919217*^9}, {
   3.694341574232729*^9, 3.694341596852769*^9}, {3.694342244717239*^9, 
   3.694342247462844*^9}, {3.694342333660995*^9, 3.694342343083412*^9}, {
   3.6943424202555304`*^9, 3.694342429299047*^9}, {3.6943424762647333`*^9, 
   3.694342484642213*^9}, {3.694342535512122*^9, 3.694342552269081*^9}, {
   3.6943425832578535`*^9, 3.694342597036641*^9}, {3.694342646046445*^9, 
   3.694342765915301*^9}, {3.694342880577859*^9, 3.694342892973568*^9}, {
   3.920005136849468*^9, 3.9200051373384686`*^9}, {3.9909526038564663`*^9, 
   3.9909526088897114`*^9}, {3.99095303486561*^9, 3.990953046670185*^9}, 
   3.990954431737709*^9, 3.990954780119398*^9, {3.9909548148734264`*^9, 
   3.9909548160267963`*^9}, 3.9909583455651093`*^9, 3.991654946804022*^9, {
   3.991656012975828*^9, 3.9916560163201466`*^9}, 3.9916581376457443`*^9, {
   3.9916582056100407`*^9, 
   3.9916582458314133`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f3069855-fa7c-4747-946c-\
9d7721b4e4b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"digitVector", "[", "n_", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Count", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"IntegerDigits", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", "d"}], "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"d", ",", "0", ",", "9"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990954433818634*^9, 3.990954433818634*^9}, 
   3.9909556919577103`*^9, {3.990955939441057*^9, 3.99095595118305*^9}, {
   3.9909563884595737`*^9, 3.990956417832445*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[39]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0ef651dc-0507-6344-b13d-f091339b3d74"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "SlideShowNavigationBar",
 CellTags->
  "SlideShowHeader",ExpressionUUID->"8f9ded65-52e4-584d-9319-42a31c3fce75"],

Cell["\<\
Based on this digit vector, the narcissistic sum can be calculated once for \
the whole permutation class. All numbers with the same digit vector produce \
the same sum.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9909549027141743`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3b224b76-2c05-644b-a490-\
9bcc0c8ba2df"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"digitVectorsOfLength", "[", "digits_", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"FrobeniusSolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "10"}], "]"}], ",", "digits"}], "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"permutationClassVectorPowerSum", "[", "v_", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "digits", "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"digits", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", "v", "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"v", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"d", "+", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "*", 
        RowBox[{"d", "^", "digits"}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", "0", ",", "9"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990954917779516*^9, 3.99095496915308*^9}, 
   3.9909559676057415`*^9, 3.990956008402666*^9, 3.9909564279496956`*^9, {
   3.9909652857593536`*^9, 3.990965325704674*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[40]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9eb5a992-6a69-cb4a-aa45-869e31661a0d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "SlideShowNavigationBar",
 CellTags->
  "SlideShowHeader",ExpressionUUID->"49044d6c-fd57-d142-8ecd-816bbeae9005"],

Cell["\<\
Instead of checking every number individually, each digit composition is \
evaluated only once.

- For each digit vector, the corresponding power sum is calculated.

- This power sum is the only possible candidate that can be narcissistic for \
this digit composition.

- The candidate is accepted only if its digit vector matches the original \
digit vector and if it lies within the selected range.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990955192223219*^9, 3.9909551936476936`*^9}, {
  3.9909581161961994`*^9, 3.990958117523615*^9}, {3.9916551013096313`*^9, 
  3.991655104467428*^9}, {3.9916553265317593`*^9, 
  3.9916553448758087`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b8960d30-c6e4-fc41-9b24-\
6675ba7fe5b3"]
}, Open  ]],

